  "title": "Nepal-Tibet Flash Floods and Himalayan Ice Melting Crisis",
  "summary": "Nepal and Tibet faced devastating flash floods and landslides due to a collapsed Himalayan glacier, resulting in over 600 deaths and 2,400 missing people. Nepal's private sectors pledged millions to disaster relief, while authorities mobilised security personnel for search and rescue operations. The floods highlighted the devastating effects of rapid melting of Himalayan ice.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Nepal and Tibet experienced over 600 deaths and 2,400 missing people from flash floods and landslides caused by a collapsed Himalayan glacier.",
