    {
      "title": "Relief as five Australians missing in Nepal-Tibet flood disaster found alive",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/01/missing-australian-found-alive-nepal-tibet-floods",
      "description": "<p>Several missing Australians have been found since Tuesday morning, bringing the total citizens unaccounted for to 38</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/31/nepal-tibet-floods-australians-missing-list-names-what-we-know-so-far-ntwnfb\">Australians missing in the Nepal floods: what we know so far</a></p></li></ul><p>A total of five Australians missing after devastating floods <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/01/nepal-china-border-area-gyirong-port-almost-entirely-cut-off-missing-australians-ntwnfb\">ravaged the Nepal-Tibet border</a> last week have been found.</p><p>Of the five Australians confirmed safe, one was found in Nepal, one in Tibet, and three outside the crisis-hit area. The total number still missing is 38.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/01/missing-australian-found-alive-nepal-tibet-floods\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-02T01:59:06"
    },
    {
      "title": "Nepal-Tibet flood deaths pass 1,000 as police ask relatives for DNA to identify victims",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/01/nepal-tibet-flood-deaths-police-relatives-dna-identification",
      "description": "<p>Relatives of missing tourists asked for blood samples and photos, as efforts continue to rescue trapped hydropower workers</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/sep/01/nepal-tibet-floods-death-toll-rescue-hydropower-tunnels-china-latest-updates\">Nepal-Tibet floods – latest updates</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/27/nepal-tibet-flash-flood-visual-guide-why-how-flooding-happened-floods-cause-reason-explained\">Visual guide: How the Nepal-Tibet flash flood unfolded</a></p></li></ul><p>Nepali rescuers have built temporary bridges to reach remote areas and dug through the ruins of hydropower projects in the Himalayas to rescue hundreds of trapped workers, as the death toll passed 1,000 nearly ⁠a week after devastating ​floods left a trail of destruction across the country’s towns and valleys.</p><p>About 600 people remain stuck in several devastated hydropower stations that have become the focus of rescue efforts. The prime ⁠minister, Balendra Shah, said more than 11,000 people had been rescued across the affected region, and power and communication lines had been restored in some areas.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/01/nepal-tibet-flood-deaths-police-relatives-dna-identification\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-01T17:32:40"
    },
    {
      "title": "Nepal flash floods: Death toll rises to 1,127, thousands still missing",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/nepal-flash-floods-death-toll-rises-to-1-127-thousands-still-missing-126090200179_1.html",
      "description": "The death toll from Nepal's devastating flash floods rose to 1,127 on Wednesday as rescuers are racing to find thousands still missing a week after the Himalayan disaster, police said.\nAccording to the Nepal Police, 348 more dead bodies were recovered from Chitwan, 217 from Nawalparasi East, 190 from Nawalparasi West and 155 from Nuwakot.\nSimilarly, 66 bodies were recovered from Gorkha, 59 from Dhading, 45 from Rasuwa, and 38 from Tanahu.\nPolice said postmortem and legal identification procedures had been completed for 1,113 bodies, while 95 had been handed over to relatives.\nDetails of 911 unidentified bodies have been uploaded to the Nepal Police website to help families identify missing relatives.\nSo far, security forces have rescued 6,541 people from the affected areas while search operations continued for 4,858 missing people, the police said.\nAuthorities have deployed 7,912 police personnel to flood-hit areas for search and rescue operations, relief distribution and the ...",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-02T04:29:08"
    }
  ]
